{"parentUuid":"6f976438-fcfe-4b05-874b-e677f50fb131","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1/ios/RheaApp","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SM75jSDJ6A3wZed5uaFsK4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good news: The SSL issue is bypassed — `xcodebuild` from CLI can reach Apple's servers fine. \n\nBad news: Validation failed with 4 issues:\n1. **Missing 120x120 app icon** (iPhone/iPod Touch)\n2. **Missing 152x152 app icon** (iPad)\n3. **iPad multitasking orientation issue** — needs `UIInterfaceOrientationPortraitUpsideDown` added to `UISupportedInterfaceOrientations`\n4. **Missing `CFBundleIconName`** — needs an asset catalog with app icons and the Info.plist key\n   \nI can fix all of these by creating an AppIcon asset catalog with the required sizes, adding the portrait upside-down orientation support, and updating Info.plist with the bundle icon name reference.\n\nFor the icons themselves, I need to generate a minimal set covering the key dimensions: 120x120, 152x152, 167x167, 180x180, and 1024x1024 for the App Store. Since Xcode 15+ can auto-generate sizes from a single 1024x1024 source, I'll create that one icon and let the build system handle the rest, then set up the asset catalog structure properly for xcodegen.\n\nCreating the icon files...\n\nNow I need to update the project configuration to reference these assets, add the bundle icon name to the Info.plist, fix the app orientation settings, and then re-archive and upload the build.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1734,"cache_read_input_tokens":100967,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1734},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":