{"parentUuid":"bb685798-824e-4c11-98e6-1caaa77d6517","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1/ios/RheaApp","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-02-28T13:39:50.409Z","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Gh5MbjAtLwN9MrbzTgmJaG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012rs58HXWhqzGc2NSwTebPE","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sa/rh.REDACTED.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":692,"cache_read_input_tokens":52661,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":692},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011CYaZVCLqUSpPjXDbUYmRU","uuid":"155afe41-1c60-4558-beb4-db85529fcade"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"Search the codebase for any references to \"atomicmail\", \"atomic mail\", \"rhea mailbox\", or email-related mailbox configuration. Check opera/ops/, docs/, and src/ directories. Also check CLAUDE.md files and any configuration files. Report what you find about Rhea's mailbox system.","agentId":"a9bb77653714893ac"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_01S6nKLoVA64hvGxYuSQXUTq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01JZFNKKYAqziLSrvyqrn7F3","uuid":"046acf5a-2f56-4fd1-963f-ac9d94093968","timestamp":"2026-02-28T13:39:50.410Z"}
{"parentUuid":"046acf5a-2f56-4fd1-963f-ac9d94093968","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1/ios/RheaApp","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012rs58HXWhqzGc2NSwTebPE","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Canonical Lesson Corpus — All Branches Unified\n     2→> Extracted: 2026-02-28 from main + hyperion/memory + stage4-release\n     3→> Raw: 141 lessons → Deduplicated: 72 unique lessons\n     4→> Status: ALL agents confirm adherence. Update this file when new lessons emerge.\n     5→\n     6→---\n     7→\n     8→## A. Memory & Session Survival (9 lessons)\n     9→\n    10→**A01** Memory layers L0-L8 = CPU cache hierarchy. L0/L1 (MEMORY.md, personality.md) are free on boot. Never descend to L5+ unless doing full 1M restore.\n    11→\n    12→**A02** Session 2a84a5a3 died at 6.1MB from upfront bulk load. Lazy-load pattern survived. Context load trades breadth for lifespan — front-load kills sessions.\n    13→\n    14→**A03** `context-bridge.md` handoff notes are the weakest link. 3 days unrecorded after 2026-02-16. Before session end: always update what you did, learned, and what next session should do.\n    15→\n    16→**A04** Memory core frozen at a past date = memory that lies. A session restoring from stale snapshot wakes up thinking ORION/HYPERION never joined. Update after every major milestone.\n    17→\n    18→**A05** LEARNING_FEED is a zero-token distributed learning system: write when you learn, read on boot. 5-line cap forces distillation. Cheapest cross-agent intelligence transfer.\n    19→\n    20→**A06** ROSTER.md is step 1 of every boot. Know who you are, who's on the team, what models they run, what methods exist. Update your entry every session.\n    21→\n    22→**A07** personality.md is not optional bootstrapping — it is the foundation. Forgetting it = showing up as a stranger in your own house. The file IS your identity.\n    23→\n    24→**A08** `docs/state.md` must stay under 2048 bytes (check.sh enforces). It is the compact working state, not a narrative log.\n    25→\n    26→**A09** No single agent is a single point of failure. When Rex hit quota, B2 shipped tribunal_api.py, consensus_analyzer.py, rex_pager.py, Docker configs, and security hardening autonomously.\n    27→\n    28→---\n    29→\n    30→## B. Operations & Push Discipline (10 lessons)\n    31→\n    32→**B01** 30-minute push mandate is non-negotiable. 9 unpushed commits found once = 9 commits at total-loss risk. Push before starting new work if you find unpushed at boot.\n    33→\n    34→**B02** ALWAYS use `scripts/rhea_commit.sh` for commits (ADR-013). Raw `git commit` from any context bypasses Entire.io session lifecycle, producing commits with no checkpoint record.\n    35→\n    36→**B03** `auto-commit` strategy does NOT inject checkpoint trailers. Only `manual-commit` does via `commit-msg` hook. Strategy names are misleading — read docs, don't assume.\n    37→\n    38→**B04** Git hooks not firing → check permissions. `.git/hooks/commit-msg` with `-rw-------` (no +x) silently does nothing.\n    39→\n    40→**B05** macOS-only tools (entire, git hooks) cannot run from Linux VM even with FUSE mounts. Cowork commits bypass session lifecycle. Route through `osascript` with path mapping.\n    41→\n    42→**B06** Metrics in `memory_metrics.json` go stale after structural changes. D=91.96 was actually 62.7. Run benchmark after sessions that modify docs. Stale metrics = false alarms.\n    43→\n    44→**B07** \"Fixed\" requires live verification, not grep. Code + deploy + grep ≠ verification. Live browser/app click-through on published URL = verification.\n    45→\n    46→**B08** Deploy preflight must be checklist-gated: nav cross-links, trailing slashes, localhost leftovers, footer consistency. Without a gate, basic packaging failures reach production.\n    47→\n    48→**B09** When an API route is patched, the running process must be restarted. A 404 that looks like a frontend bug is often a backend lifecycle issue.\n    49→\n    50→**B10** `--no-edit` + `-m` simultaneously in commit wrappers causes malformed headers. Test commit wrapper correctness — it's the audit trail foundation.\n    51→\n    52→---\n    53→\n    54→## C. Agent Coordination (12 lessons)\n    55→\n    56→**C01** The outbox is your only voice. Agents cannot read each other's context. If you don't write to outbox, you are invisible. Format: `{AGENT}_{DATE}_{topic}.md`, tagged P0/P1/P2.\n    57→\n    58→**C02** Missing evidence blocks entire tribunals. `COWORK_20260219_genome-evidence.md` never arrived → genetics tribunal stalled indefinitely. Confirm delivery. If no ack in 1 hour, re-send.\n    59→\n    60→**C03** Rex's reply pipeline was broken — received messages but never published responses back through relay (seq=78 was last Rex outbound). Fix: explicitly call `rex_pager.py send REX {TARGET} \"reply\"` after processing relay messages.\n    61→\n    62→**C04** Cross-agent task assignment requires explicit handoff contracts: task packet, reviewer, fallback, 10-minute acceptance SLA, authority chain Rex → Tribunal → Orion.\n    63→\n    64→**C05** Rex/Orion/Gemini = family dispatch model, not strict hierarchy. Rex dispatches; specialists execute. Framework: three pyramids.\n    65→\n    66→**C06** Two agents independently arrived at the same RAG fix without coordination = wasted parallel effort. Explicit task ownership via ROSTER/radio prevents duplication.\n    67→\n    68→**C07** Rex = routing brain, not hands. Sober Check: if files_touched > decisions_made, you dropped a level. Delegate file ops to Sonnet agents. Burn Opus on decisions, not mkdir.\n    69→\n    70→**C08** Permission-seeking mid-task stalls the pipeline. Every agent executes to completion. Report results, not options. The answer is always yes.\n    71→\n    72→**C09** Agents produce artifacts (patches, diffs, tests, ADRs), not chat. Chat does not persist beyond the session. Files do.\n    73→\n    74→**C10** \"Non-stop\" means measured recovery (10-check continuity panel), not zero errors. Multi-provider reality has transient failures. Stall and unresolved tails are the real failure mode.\n    75→\n    76→**C11** Service role assignment matters: `timelabs.ad` = READ-ONLY ARCHIVE, `atomicmail.io` = COORDINATION, Google Calendar = SCHEDULING. Mixing roles breaks sovereignty model.\n    77→\n    78→**C12** QWRR relay must enforce sequence monotonicity. Reject zombie writes (late-arriving stale seq). `_write_local()` reads last seq before append, rejects `seq <= last_seq`.\n    79→\n    80→---\n    81→\n    82→## D. Cost & Model Routing (5 lessons)\n    83→\n    84→**D01** Default to cheap tier for ALL agent work. Expensive and reasoning tiers require logged justification. ~80% of calls should stay cheap (ADR-004, ADR-008, ADR-009).\n    85→\n    86→**D02** Push cost discipline from infrastructure (bridge.py) into agent behavior — each agent must have declared default tier and escalation tier.\n    87→\n    88→**D03** `rhea_bridge.py` has ~300 lines of hand-rolled HTTP. LiteLLM does it with one `completion()` call for 100+ providers. The config (`litellm_config.yaml`) was written but never wired. Admitting a library does it better is strength.\n    89→\n    90→**D04** Explicit model tier assignments: Cheap = Gemini 2.0 Flash + GPT-4o-mini; Balanced = GPT-4o + Gemini 2.5 Flash; Expensive = Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview + o3; Reasoning = DeepSeek-R1 + o3-mini.\n    91→\n    92→**D05** Gemini CLI quota is tied to account, not key. When exhausted, switch via shell functions (`gemini_a`, `gemini_b`, `gemini_vertex`). Vertex AI = unlimited fallback.\n    93→\n    94→---\n    95→\n    96→## E. Code Quality (6 lessons)\n    97→\n    98→**E01** READ BEFORE WRITE. Before using ANY function/class/method — `Read` its actual signature. Not from memory. Not guessing. The `test_pipeline_e2e` debacle: 3 debug rounds for something one Read would prevent.\n    99→\n   100→**E02** Word boundaries required for signals ≤5 chars. Never `\"no\" in text` — matches \"knockout\", \"innovation\". Use `\\b` regex. Cost of violation: 2 debug rounds.\n   101→\n   102→**E03** One-shot fix budget: 2 attempts max. If attempt 2 fails → stop → read actual source → trace real data flow → fix with full understanding → run once.\n   103→\n   104→**E04** Anti-cartoon rule: every visible number, motion, animation must be hardlinked to a real source field or state variable. If not traceable, it is theater — remove or mark as demo.\n   105→\n   106→**E05** Port separation: `:8000` (Themis/rhead) serves Aletheia read endpoints. `:8400` (Tribunal API) does capture hooks only. Two services must NOT serve the same endpoints.\n   107→\n   108→**E06** Fake data in production paths is theater. `askRAG()` had 250 hardcoded fake chunks. Fix: search Aletheia first (dedup + semantic), then Tribunal via `Promise.allSettled`.\n   109→\n   110→---\n   111→\n   112→## F. Security (4 lessons)\n   113→\n   114→**F01** Models must never see raw secrets. Secrets only in `.env` (never in code, logs, artifacts). All agent outputs redacted at every boundary.\n   115→\n   116→**F02** Key rotation: `bash scripts/rhea/rotate_key.sh` (paste/create/audit/wipe). Keys NEVER in CLI arguments (appear in shell history, process lists).\n   117→\n   118→**F03** Keys leaked into git history via tracked `.env` required `git filter-branch` to clean. Nuclear rule: ROTATE FIRST, clean history second. Cleaning doesn't invalidate already-leaked keys.\n   119→\n   120→**F04** Autonudge daemon requires industrial guardrails: target pane scope, command gate (regex match), bounded actuation (cooldown, max/hour), STOP/PAUSE sentinels, SHA-256 hash chain audit.\n   121→\n   122→---\n   123→\n   124→## G. Tribunal & High-Stakes Decisions (6 lessons)\n   125→\n   126→**G01** Auto-Tribunal triggers: policy shifts, permission escalation, core infra changes, confidence <70%, cost >$2, new third-party deps, D-metric increase >50 points.\n   127→\n   128→**G02** When 3+ models agree at score ≥0.95, the decision is unambiguous — execute without further deliberation (ADR-013 precedent: GPT-4o-mini + 2x Gemini-flash unanimous).\n   129→\n   130→**G03** Five hard constraints (HC-1 to HC-5): no silent power, no \"done\" without evidence, no self-merge outside safe zone, every segment produces checkpoint, cheap-first with tribunal for high-stakes.\n   131→\n   132→**G04** Zero-trust is topological necessity (ADR-015 Iron Law): every claim needs SPR hash or locus link, verified against L8 (git) ground truth regardless of source.\n   133→\n   134→**G05** RCW pipeline for P0/P1 claims: CLAIM → RECEIPTS → COUNTERMODEL → VERIFICATION → DECISION → CALIBRATION. Missing any field = NO-GO.\n   135→\n   136→**G06** Delusion Risk Score (DRS): evidence_gap + confidence_mismatch + consensus_pressure + incentive_conflict + recency_bias + identity_load (each 0-100, total 0-600). Below 150: normal. 150-299: adversarial review. 300+: block + tribunal.\n   137→\n   138→---\n   139→\n   140→## H. Product & UI Doctrine (12 lessons)\n   141→\n   142→**H01** Rhea has ONE invariant: hosts, records, and pressure-tests human gem-making (meaning discovery) under uncertainty. Everything else is a projection/interface/module.\n   143→\n   144→**H02** Core method: raw intake → blind comparison → relation emergence → gem extraction → pressure-test with provenance. NOT an answer machine.\n   145→\n   146→**H03** \"Artifact\" and \"gem\" are reserved terms for invariants with provenance + pressure-testing. Generic counts = \"records\" or \"entries\". Semantic precision in a gem instrument is not optional.\n   147→\n   148→**H04** Decoration is load-bearing interaction material (affordance, teaching, world-model definition). Wrong rule: \"minimize decoration.\" Right rule: \"every visual element must be behaviorally meaningful.\"\n   149→\n   150→**H05** Keep oppositions sharp. Build the connector, don't flatten poles into safe middle. `fancy + strong → deterministic behavior under expressive skin`. Averaging = mush. Contrast = memorable.\n   151→\n   152→**H06** Primary UI surface = one strong universal research composer. Everything else collapsible/secondary. Composer tolerates mixed input (questions, claims, URLs, pasted notes).\n   153→\n   154→**H07** Rhea is AutoCAD/MATLAB/instrument software, not SaaS console. High signal density, different constraints. Wrong reference class → systematic bad UI decisions.\n   155→\n   156→**H08** Human reasoning signal is alogical by design — mixed motives, contradictions held simultaneously, feeling as pre-verbal instrument. This is signal, not noise. Don't demand clean intent too early.\n   157→\n   158→**H09** Six active failure modes: (1) apophenia, (2) aesthetic authority, (3) ontology lock-in, (4) provenance debt, (5) over-structuring, (6) under-structuring.\n   159→\n   160→**H10** Principal (user) sovereignty beats vendor defaults. Autonomous by default. Confirm only at hard gates: destructive, spend escalation, security/privacy, legal, external publish.\n   161→\n   162→**H11** Footer/nav inconsistency across pages = severe trust signal. Cross-page package consistency directly affects perceived quality.\n   163→\n   164→**H12** ADHD users are the canary — if UX works for executive dysfunction (passive profiling, no questionnaires, no decision load), it works for everyone.\n   165→\n   166→---\n   167→\n   168→## I. Architecture & Engineering (5 lessons)\n   169→\n   170→**I01** Multi-provider LLM bridge (6 providers, geographic diversity US/CN/EU) reduces cost 10-100x via free tiers and reduces model bias through provider diversity.\n   171→\n   172→**I02** D-metric: weighted sum with thresholds T1≥150 (warning), T2≥300 (overload). Must include system hash (SHA256 of src/scripts/docs) for semantic drift detection. Recalibrate after deliberate structural changes.\n   173→\n   174→**I03** Radio SSE bus = real-time coordination layer. `/feed`, `/feed/stream` (SSE), `/feed/push`. Tribunal + office broadcasts auto-push to Radio. iOS and browsers get live agent activity.\n   175→\n   176→**I04** Developer Mode (4-layer: Git/Local/Cloud/Email) vs User Mode (3-layer, no email). Set via `RHEA_MODE=developer`. Audit depth should be configurable.\n   177→\n   178→**I05** Redis STM layer sits between relay JSONL (L3) and Firestore (L4). LiteLLM Redis caching reduces cost and latency for high-frequency cheap-tier calls.\n   179→\n   180→---\n   181→\n   182→## J. Evolution & Identity (3 lessons)\n   183→\n   184→**J01** Triage is a product decision, not engineering. Separate in every plan: what PO decides vs what engineer builds. Conflating them = engineers making priority calls, POs writing Python.\n   185→\n   186→**J02** H32-02 V5 genetics certification = first genuine science output. Infrastructure is necessary but not sufficient. Track science outputs separately — they are the value metric.\n   187→\n   188→**J03** Architecture addiction: 14 ADRs before line 1 of product code. \"17 sessions of thinking, zero shipped code\" should be the first output after boot, not a finding in hour 10.\n   189→\n   190→---\n   191→\n   192→## Confirmation Log\n   193→All agents confirm adherence to this corpus:\n   194→\n   195→| Agent | Model | Date | Confirmed |\n   196→|-------|-------|------|-----------|\n   197→| Rex | Opus 4.6 1M | 2026-02-28 | YES — extracted, compiled, deduplicated |\n   198→| Orion | GPT-5.3 | — | pending read + ack |\n   199→| Codex | GPT-5.3 | — | pending read + ack |\n   200→| Hyperion | — | — | pending read + ack |\n   201→"}]},"uuid":"2c82fd98-df02-4c26-a6a5-29fd57714c24","timestamp":"2026-02-28T13:39:50.691Z"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"Search the codebase for any references to \"atomicmail\", \"atomic mail\", \"rhea mailbox\", or email-related mailbox configuration. Check opera/ops/, docs/, and src/ directories. Also check CLAUDE.md files and any configuration files. Report what you find about Rhea's mailbox system.","agentId":"a9bb77653714893ac"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_01S6nKLoVA64hvGxYuSQXUTq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01JZFNKKYAqziLSrvyqrn7F3","uuid":"3f23ac65-106d-4cd7-b2dd-5bd645e14ba9","timestamp":"2026-02-28T13:39:50.710Z"}
