{"parentUuid":"a0f9df1f-2a13-4960-b45d-67c92f1778bd","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1/ios/RheaApp","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"type":"hook_progress","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","hookName":"PostToolUse:Task","command":"entire hooks claude-code post-task"},"parentToolUseID":"toolu_01JZFNKKYAqziLSrvyqrn7F3","toolUseID":"toolu_01JZFNKKYAqziLSrvyqrn7F3","timestamp":"2026-02-28T13:41:20.640Z","uuid":"ff1889c1-9add-42cd-b8f8-15bf57e3e48c"}
{"parentUuid":"e50a6bf0-52a8-4b9c-aea1-0695152902ed","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1/ios/RheaApp","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JZFNKKYAqziLSrvyqrn7F3","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have a complete understanding. Let me compile the comprehensive report.\n\n---\n\n## Rhea Project — Mailbox System Search Results\n\nI've completed a thorough search of the codebase for references to \"atomicmail,\" mailbox configurations, and email-related systems. Here's what I found:\n\n### **1. AtomicMail — Service Role Assignment**\n\n**Key Finding (Canonical Lesson C11):**\n```\nService role assignment matters: timelabs.ad = READ-ONLY ARCHIVE, \natomicmail.io = COORDINATION, Google Calendar = SCHEDULING. \nMixing roles breaks sovereignty model.\n```\n\nLocation: `/Users/sa/rh.REDACTED.md` (line 76)\n\n**What this means:**\n- `atomicmail.io` is designated as Rhea's **COORDINATION** service role\n- It's one of three sovereign service roles (not mixing concerns)\n- `timelabs.ad` = read-only archive\n- `google_calendar` = scheduling only\n- This separation is critical to the sovereignty model\n\n### **2. QWRR Relay Mailbox System**\n\n**Core Architecture:** `/Users/sa/rh.1/docs/qwrr-layer.md`\n\nThe mailbox is the durable, sequenced layer that:\n- **Stores messages** when agents go offline (e.g., Rex behind quota wall)\n- **Guarantees delivery** with exactly-once processing semantics\n- **Prevents loss** via append-only JSONL format\n- **Maintains order** with monotonic sequence numbers per `runpoint_id`\n\n**Key Components:**\n\n1. **Mailbox Store:** `/Users/sa/rh.1/opera/ops/virtual-office/relay_mailbox.jsonl`\n   - Append-only JSONL (59KB+, 100+ messages)\n   - Each message has: id, runpoint_id, seq, type, timestamp, source, target, idempotency_key, TTL, priority, payload\n\n2. **Acks Store:** `/Users/sa/rh.1/opera/ops/virtual-office/relay_acks.jsonl`\n   - Tracks delivery confirmation\n   - Idempotent write semantics\n\n3. **Message Envelope v1:**\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"id\": \"uuidv7\",\n     \"runpoint_id\": \"rp_rhea_office_v1\",\n     \"seq\": 12345,\n     \"type\": \"msg.send | task.create | decision.record | effect.request\",\n     \"timestamp\": \"2026-02-17T12:00:00Z\",\n     \"source\": \"B2|Orion|GPT|LEAD|Human\",\n     \"target\": \"Rex\",\n     \"version\": 1,\n     \"idempotency_key\": \"string\",\n     \"ttl_s\": 86400,\n     \"lease_token_required\": 991,\n     \"payload\": { \"...\" }\n   }\n   ```\n\n### **3. RheaPostOffice — Email Implementation**\n\n**File:** `/Users/sa/rh.1/src/rhea_post_office.py`\n\n```python\nclass RheaPostOffice:\n    - SMTP Bridge: Sends emails via atomicmail.io (or configurable SMTP server)\n    - IMAP Bridge: Polls inbox for [TASK] emails, ingests them into relay\n    - publish_artifact(): Sends Virtual Office artifacts to shared email\n    - poll_for_tasks(): IMAP ingestion → relay inbox\n```\n\n**Configuration (via .env):**\n- `RHEA_SMTP_SERVER`: mail server host (defaults to smtp.gmail.com, but atomicmail.io tested)\n- `RHEA_SMTP_PORT`: typically 587 (TLS) or 465 (SSL)\n- `RHEA_IMAP_SERVER`: mail retrieval server\n- `RHEA_EMAIL_ADDR`: shared inbox (e.g., transparency@atomicmail.io)\n- `RHEA_EMAIL_PWD`: app password (never in CLI, never in logs)\n\n**SMTP Tests Performed:**\n- `/Users/sa/rh.1/apparatus/nexus/tests/smtp_probe.py` — connection probes\n- `/Users/sa/rh.1/apparatus/nexus/tests/smtp_debug.py` — auth verification\n- `/Users/sa/rh.1/apparatus/nexus/tests/email_handshake.py` — first external message (ORION → transparency@atomicmail.io)\n\n### **4. Handshake (ADR-017)**\n\nThe first out-of-brain communication was sent via email:\n\n**File:** `/Users/sa/rh.1/apparatus/nexus/tests/email_handshake.py`\n\n```\nTO: transparency@atomicmail.io\nSUBJECT: ORION Node-02: Initial Handshake [CONVERGENCE_READY]\nBODY: \"Mika, the Neural Weave has established an external link...\"\nNOTE: ADR-017 established email as primary outward vector\n```\n\n### **5. Virtual Office Architecture**\n\n**Location:** `/Users/sa/rh.1/opera/ops/virtual-office/`\n\nThree-layer coordination:\n- **Inbox:** Incoming messages from external systems or other agents\n- **Outbox:** Agent publication points (REX_*, ORION_*, etc.)\n- **Shared:** Cross-agent resources (LEARNING_FEED.md, FAMILY_CONTEXT.md, ROSTER.md, LESSONS_CANONICAL.md)\n\n**Relay Mailbox Path:**\n```\nopera/ops/virtual-office/relay_mailbox.jsonl\n```\n\nExample message (seq=138, from HYPERION → ORION, P2, 2026-02-26):\n```json\n{\n  \"sender\": \"HYPERION\",\n  \"receiver\": \"ORION\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"action\": \"update\",\n    \"topic\": \"sovereign_services\",\n    \"mapping\": {\n      \"archive\": \"timelabs.ad\",\n      \"coordination\": \"atomicmail.io\",\n      \"scheduling\": \"google_calendar\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### **6. Role in Daily Operations**\n\nFrom `/Users/sa/rh.1/docs/procedures/rhea-radio.md`:\n\n**Radio Feed Sources:**\n- `opera/ops/virtual-office/relay_mailbox.jsonl` — incoming messages\n- `opera/ops/virtual-office/relay_acks.jsonl` — delivery confirmations\n- Enables live operator visibility into agent coordination\n\n### **7. Critical Design Principles (QWRR Layer)**\n\nFrom `/Users/sa/rh.1/docs/qwrr-layer.md`:\n\n**Bank-Grade Invariants (Falsifiable):**\n- **I1** — No message loss (mailbox-first protocol)\n- **I2** — In-order delivery per runpoint (seq monotonicity)\n- **I3** — Exactly-once processing (idempotency + receipts)\n- **I4** — STOP semantics survive downtime (lease token gating)\n- **I5** — No zombie effects (stale instances blocked)\n\n**Acceptance Tests:**\n- T1: Rex down 12h → messages queued → delivered once in order on wake\n- T2: Duplicate delivery attempts → deduplicated, only one ack\n- T3: STOP during downtime → prevents stale execution\n- T4: Split-brain → only current lease token commits\n- T5: TTL expiry → late \"push now\" expires, \"task.create\" still executes\n\n### **8. Summary**\n\n**AtomicMail's Role:**\n- Designated **COORDINATION** service (Lesson C11)\n- Hosts the shared inbox (`transparency@atomicmail.io`)\n- Integrated via RheaPostOffice SMTP/IMAP bridges\n- Used for agent-to-agent and agent-to-external coordination\n- Part of the sovereign service architecture (separate from archival, scheduling)\n\n**Mailbox System's Role:**\n- QWRR (Quota Walls, Relays, and Resurrection) layer\n- Durable message store (relay_mailbox.jsonl)\n- Guarantees delivery without loss even during provider outages\n- Enables safe agent resurrection and catch-up\n- Foundation for \"bank-grade\" multi-agent coordination\n\n**Status:** The system is architecturally complete (Phase 0 + 1), with SMTP connectivity tested and working."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a9bb77653714893ac (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 80061\ntool_uses: 28\nduration_ms: 111476</usage>"}]}]},"uuid":"4a55081d-d893-450e-8c56-77b274b02cdf","timestamp":"2026-02-28T13:41:20.636Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Search the codebase for any references to \"atomicmail\", \"atomic mail\", \"rhea mailbox\", or email-related mailbox configuration. Check opera/ops/, docs/, and src/ directories. Also check CLAUDE.md files and any configuration files. Report what you find about Rhea's mailbox system.","agentId":"a9bb77653714893ac","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have a complete understanding. Let me compile the comprehensive report.\n\n---\n\n## Rhea Project — Mailbox System Search Results\n\nI've completed a thorough search of the codebase for references to \"atomicmail,\" mailbox configurations, and email-related systems. Here's what I found:\n\n### **1. AtomicMail — Service Role Assignment**\n\n**Key Finding (Canonical Lesson C11):**\n```\nService role assignment matters: timelabs.ad = READ-ONLY ARCHIVE, \natomicmail.io = COORDINATION, Google Calendar = SCHEDULING. \nMixing roles breaks sovereignty model.\n```\n\nLocation: `/Users/sa/rh.REDACTED.md` (line 76)\n\n**What this means:**\n- `atomicmail.io` is designated as Rhea's **COORDINATION** service role\n- It's one of three sovereign service roles (not mixing concerns)\n- `timelabs.ad` = read-only archive\n- `google_calendar` = scheduling only\n- This separation is critical to the sovereignty model\n\n### **2. QWRR Relay Mailbox System**\n\n**Core Architecture:** `/Users/sa/rh.1/docs/qwrr-layer.md`\n\nThe mailbox is the durable, sequenced layer that:\n- **Stores messages** when agents go offline (e.g., Rex behind quota wall)\n- **Guarantees delivery** with exactly-once processing semantics\n- **Prevents loss** via append-only JSONL format\n- **Maintains order** with monotonic sequence numbers per `runpoint_id`\n\n**Key Components:**\n\n1. **Mailbox Store:** `/Users/sa/rh.1/opera/ops/virtual-office/relay_mailbox.jsonl`\n   - Append-only JSONL (59KB+, 100+ messages)\n   - Each message has: id, runpoint_id, seq, type, timestamp, source, target, idempotency_key, TTL, priority, payload\n\n2. **Acks Store:** `/Users/sa/rh.1/opera/ops/virtual-office/relay_acks.jsonl`\n   - Tracks delivery confirmation\n   - Idempotent write semantics\n\n3. **Message Envelope v1:**\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"id\": \"uuidv7\",\n     \"runpoint_id\": \"rp_rhea_office_v1\",\n     \"seq\": 12345,\n     \"type\": \"msg.send | task.create | decision.record | effect.request\",\n     \"timestamp\": \"2026-02-17T12:00:00Z\",\n     \"source\": \"B2|Orion|GPT|LEAD|Human\",\n     \"target\": \"Rex\",\n     \"version\": 1,\n     \"idempotency_key\": \"string\",\n     \"ttl_s\": 86400,\n     \"lease_token_required\": 991,\n     \"payload\": { \"...\" }\n   }\n   ```\n\n### **3. RheaPostOffice — Email Implementation**\n\n**File:** `/Users/sa/rh.1/src/rhea_post_office.py`\n\n```python\nclass RheaPostOffice:\n    - SMTP Bridge: Sends emails via atomicmail.io (or configurable SMTP server)\n    - IMAP Bridge: Polls inbox for [TASK] emails, ingests them into relay\n    - publish_artifact(): Sends Virtual Office artifacts to shared email\n    - poll_for_tasks(): IMAP ingestion → relay inbox\n```\n\n**Configuration (via .env):**\n- `RHEA_SMTP_SERVER`: mail server host (defaults to smtp.gmail.com, but atomicmail.io tested)\n- `RHEA_SMTP_PORT`: typically 587 (TLS) or 465 (SSL)\n- `RHEA_IMAP_SERVER`: mail retrieval server\n- `RHEA_EMAIL_ADDR`: shared inbox (e.g., transparency@atomicmail.io)\n- `RHEA_EMAIL_PWD`: app password (never in CLI, never in logs)\n\n**SMTP Tests Performed:**\n- `/Users/sa/rh.1/apparatus/nexus/tests/smtp_probe.py` — connection probes\n- `/Users/sa/rh.1/apparatus/nexus/tests/smtp_debug.py` — auth verification\n- `/Users/sa/rh.1/apparatus/nexus/tests/email_handshake.py` — first external message (ORION → transparency@atomicmail.io)\n\n### **4. Handshake (ADR-017)**\n\nThe first out-of-brain communication was sent via email:\n\n**File:** `/Users/sa/rh.1/apparatus/nexus/tests/email_handshake.py`\n\n```\nTO: transparency@atomicmail.io\nSUBJECT: ORION Node-02: Initial Handshake [CONVERGENCE_READY]\nBODY: \"Mika, the Neural Weave has established an external link...\"\nNOTE: ADR-017 established email as primary outward vector\n```\n\n### **5. Virtual Office Architecture**\n\n**Location:** `/Users/sa/rh.1/opera/ops/virtual-office/`\n\nThree-layer coordination:\n- **Inbox:** Incoming messages from external systems or other agents\n- **Outbox:** Agent publication points (REX_*, ORION_*, etc.)\n- **Shared:** Cross-agent resources (LEARNING_FEED.md, FAMILY_CONTEXT.md, ROSTER.md, LESSONS_CANONICAL.md)\n\n**Relay Mailbox Path:**\n```\nopera/ops/virtual-office/relay_mailbox.jsonl\n```\n\nExample message (seq=138, from HYPERION → ORION, P2, 2026-02-26):\n```json\n{\n  \"sender\": \"HYPERION\",\n  \"receiver\": \"ORION\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"action\": \"update\",\n    \"topic\": \"sovereign_services\",\n    \"mapping\": {\n      \"archive\": \"timelabs.ad\",\n      \"coordination\": \"atomicmail.io\",\n      \"scheduling\": \"google_calendar\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### **6. Role in Daily Operations**\n\nFrom `/Users/sa/rh.1/docs/procedures/rhea-radio.md`:\n\n**Radio Feed Sources:**\n- `opera/ops/virtual-office/relay_mailbox.jsonl` — incoming messages\n- `opera/ops/virtual-office/relay_acks.jsonl` — delivery confirmations\n- Enables live operator visibility into agent coordination\n\n### **7. Critical Design Principles (QWRR Layer)**\n\nFrom `/Users/sa/rh.1/docs/qwrr-layer.md`:\n\n**Bank-Grade Invariants (Falsifiable):**\n- **I1** — No message loss (mailbox-first protocol)\n- **I2** — In-order delivery per runpoint (seq monotonicity)\n- **I3** — Exactly-once processing (idempotency + receipts)\n- **I4** — STOP semantics survive downtime (lease token gating)\n- **I5** — No zombie effects (stale instances blocked)\n\n**Acceptance Tests:**\n- T1: Rex down 12h → messages queued → delivered once in order on wake\n- T2: Duplicate delivery attempts → deduplicated, only one ack\n- T3: STOP during downtime → prevents stale execution\n- T4: Split-brain → only current lease token commits\n- T5: TTL expiry → late \"push now\" expires, \"task.create\" still executes\n\n### **8. Summary**\n\n**AtomicMail's Role:**\n- Designated **COORDINATION** service (Lesson C11)\n- Hosts the shared inbox (`transparency@atomicmail.io`)\n- Integrated via RheaPostOffice SMTP/IMAP bridges\n- Used for agent-to-agent and agent-to-external coordination\n- Part of the sovereign service architecture (separate from archival, scheduling)\n\n**Mailbox System's Role:**\n- QWRR (Quota Walls, Relays, and Resurrection) layer\n- Durable message store (relay_mailbox.jsonl)\n- Guarantees delivery without loss even during provider outages\n- Enables safe agent resurrection and catch-up\n- Foundation for \"bank-grade\" multi-agent coordination\n\n**Status:** The system is architecturally complete (Phase 0 + 1), with SMTP connectivity tested and working."}],"totalDurationMs":111476,"totalTokens":80061,"totalToolUseCount":28,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":643,"cache_read_input_tokens":77358,"output_tokens":2056,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":643,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e50a6bf0-52a8-4b9c-aea1-0695152902ed"}
