{"parentUuid":"c8349efc-9a43-4308-8672-52a1f8c79cb0","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1/ios/RheaApp","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01K6gQyFzj9KRtTRWkJCvPeS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Build #4 uploaded to App Store Connect.** Upload succeeded, package is processing.\n\nNow about atomicmail — the search found it:\n\n**AtomicMail (`atomicmail.io`)** is Rhea's designated **COORDINATION** service (Lesson C11 in `LESSONS_CANONICAL.md`):\n- `transparency@atomicmail.io` = shared inbox\n- Integrated via `src/rhea_post_office.py` (SMTP/IMAP bridges)  \n- Service role separation: `timelabs.ad` = archive, `atomicmail.io` = coordination, `google_calendar` = scheduling\n- First external handshake was ORION → `transparency@atomicmail.io` (ADR-017)\n- The relay mailbox (`relay_mailbox.jsonl`) is the durable backing store — QWRR layer with bank-grade invariants\n\nThe build should appear in App Store Connect → TestFlight within ~5-15 minutes as it processes. Once it shows up, you can add yourself as an internal tester and install immediately — no Beta App Review needed for internal testers.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe Xcode Organizer failed on SSL to `developerservices3.apple.com` during cloud re-signing, but the CLI-exported IPA was already Distribution-signed. Using `xcodebuild -exportArchive` with `destination: upload` in the ExportOptions plist bypasses the Organizer entirely — it validates, uploads, and the binary is already properly signed. This is the more reliable path for CI/CD pipelines.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1125,"cache_read_input_tokens":111283,"output_tokens":398,"server_tool_use":{"web_se