{"parentUuid":"307e24ab-199f-4b3f-8921-3780b7194909","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DzdqyJ1R3TfBkmVKNeRP2P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the issues:\n\n1. **Governor is blank/white**: It fetches from `/agents/status` which is the unified endpoint we added. The response might not match the expected `GovernorUnifiedResponse` format. Let me check if that endpoint is working.\n\n2. **Dialog needs wiring**: Currently calls `/office/send`, needs to call `/dialog`.\n\n3. **API Base URL is `localhost:8400`**: On the real device, this won't work unless the user has changed it in Settings. The device needs to point to the actual server IP. But that's a settings thing the user can configure.\n\nWait - the screenshots show the app running. If it's on a real device, `localhost:8400` won't reach the Mac's server. \n\nThe Radio tab is showing data though, so either the user configured the API URL in Settings or there's something else going on. Let me trace through what the Governor endpoint is actually returning to understand why it's blank.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4747,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1164,"cache_read_input_tokens":62205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1164},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CYagyUHPVEqP7C7qv6w9m","type":"assistant","uuid":"b3727698-1c7a-4f76-a165-2fa1c2cf5c73","timestamp":"2026-02-28T15:18:19.960Z"}
