{"parentUuid":"d38b7fcb-d879-48fe-891c-7fba06a086ac","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01M2w36jR9U1hZ5HihwtnXoo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Two issues found:\n\n1. **`/dialog` endpoint doesn't exist** — means the server running doesn't have the code I added last session. Need to restart the server.\n\n2. **Governor decoding fails** — the response has extra fields like `lease_token`, `lease_expired`, `lease_expires_at`, `last_feed` that aren't in the `AgentStatus` struct. In Swift, by default `Codable` requires all keys in JSON to map to properties. BUT actually, Swift's `Codable` by default ignores unknown keys — it only fails if required properties are missing. Let me think...\n\nActually wait, Swift's `JSONDecoder` by default does NOT fail on unknown keys — it just ignores them. \n\nSo extra fields shouldn't be the issue. The Governor tab is showing a completely white screen with no navigation title, which suggests either the background color isn't rendering properly on the device, or there's a decoding failure happening silently. The `_ts` field with an underscore should work fine with Codable since it's explicitly defined. Let me check if the `Pow` import is even available in the Swift Playground environment.\n\nActually, looking at the screenshots more carefully - the white screen in screenshot 5 is definitely the Governor tab, and the other tabs are working fine. The most likely explanation is that `localhost:8400` is unreachable from the phone since it's pointing to the Mac's server, so the fetch fails silently and leaves `agents` empty. That should trigger the `ContentUnavailableView` with \"No Data\" text, but I'm not seeing that either.\n\nThe real culprit is probably App Transport Security - HTTP connections to `localhost:8400` are blocked on real devices unless explicitly allowed in the Info.plist, whereas the simulator might have different security rules.\n\nBut wait, if the Radio tab works fine, then the network connection itself isn't the issue. The Governor tab specifically is showing a blank white screen, which suggests either a crash in that view's code (possibly related to the Pow import) or something specific to how that tab renders its content.\n\nLooking at the tab bar across the screenshots, the white screen is definitely the Governor tab selected, so the problem is isolated to that view's implementation. The white screen is likely because the device can't reach the server, so the agent list is empty and shows a ContentUnavailableView with light-mode colors against a white background — the `.toolbarColorScheme(.dark)` only affects the toolbar, not the content itself.\n\nLet me focus on what the user actually wants: getting Dialog working. I'll wire up DialogView to hit the `/dialog` endpoint, restart the server, and add `.preferredColorScheme(.dark)` to the Governor view to fix the background issue properly.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5935,"cache_read_input_tokens":63369,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5935},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CYah1Vd49Mwm9R2hd9KHy","type":"assistant","uuid":"7f359a80-bf2a-465e-99ff-212ee1970968","timestamp":"2026-02-28T15:19:07.467Z"}
