{"parentUuid":"32b08853-d437-45c7-8e61-e3cd652e2318","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WW7sCH5Bw9RhSXGh9r4mmv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Play app SwiftUI component library cards buttons navigation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - Toni77777/awesome-swiftui-libraries: :rocket: Awesome SwiftUI Libraries\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Toni77777/awesome-swiftui-libraries\"},{\"title\":\"Awesome SwiftUI Libraries List - DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/toni777772/awesome-swiftui-libraries-list-3agc\"},{\"title\":\"Build a Reusable SwiftUI Component Library - DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/sebastienlato/build-a-reusable-swiftui-component-library-15i3\"},{\"title\":\"Build your own button component library in SwiftUI from scratch - DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/calin_crist/build-your-own-button-component-library-in-swiftui-from-scratch-5g9m\"},{\"title\":\"SwiftUI Card View with Navigation | by Christopher Bell | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@christopher.a.REDACTED\"},{\"title\":\"Awesome SwiftUI Libraries. · Anton Paliakov DevBlog\",\"url\":\"https://tonidevblog.com/posts/awesome-swiftui-libraries/\"},{\"title\":\"Designing a single card view - a free Hacking with iOS: SwiftUI Edition tutorial\",\"url\":\"https://www.hackingwithswift.com/books/ios-swiftui/designing-a-single-card-view\"},{\"title\":\"Build Your Own Button Component Library From Scratch in SwiftUI | by Calin-Cristian Ciubotariu | Better Programming\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/better-programming/build-your-own-button-component-library-from-scratch-in-swiftui-14cfa2f0036b\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - matteocrippa/awesome-swift: A collaborative list of awesome Swift libraries and resources. Feel free to contribute!\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/matteocrippa/awesome-swift\"},{\"title\":\"Explore SwiftUI - Visual Library for SwiftUI Components | Explore SwiftUI\",\"url\":\"https://exploreswiftui.com/\"}]\n\nHere are the search results for SwiftUI component libraries featuring cards, buttons, and navigation:\n\n## Key SwiftUI Component Libraries\n\n**Card Components:**\n- DeckKit is a tiny library that helps you create card-based apps in SwiftUI\n- SlideOverCard - A SwiftUI card view, made great for setup interactions\n- SwiftUI-CardStackView - A easy-to-use SwiftUI view for Tinder like cards on iOS, macOS & watchOS\n\n**Button Components:**\n- buttoncraft - Craft that perfect SwiftUI button effect\n- CUIExpandableButton - A SwiftUI button that expands to show more content\n- FloatingButton - Easily customizable floating button menu created with SwiftUI\n\n**Navigation Solutions:**\n- Coordinator - A declarative navigation API for SwiftUI\n- FlowStacks - FlowStacks allows you to hoist SwiftUI navigation and presentation state into a Coordinator\n- NavigationStack - An alternative SwiftUI NavigationView implementing classic stack-based navigation giving also some more control on animations and programmatic navigation\n- Router - Router is a library that assists with SwiftUI view transitions\n\nThese libraries provide comprehensive solutions for building modern, interactive SwiftUI applications with reusable component patterns for cards, buttons, and navigation flows.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"60fb05a7-f1b1-4a00-a5b5-eda22b8274fb","timestamp":"2026-02-28T15:28:03.264Z"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"Research Play.app (createwithplay.com / play.app) — the iOS native design tool that exports SwiftUI. I need to know:\n\n1. What UI component library does Play provide? (cards, buttons, navigation, lists, etc.)\n2. How does the SwiftUI export work — what format, any dependencies?\n3. Can Play components be used in a Swift Playground App (.swiftpm) project directly?\n4. Any known limitations of Play's exported SwiftUI code?\n5. Does Play have a package/framework that can be added as a dependency, or is it purely copy-paste export?\n\nFocus on practical integration details, not marketing. Return concise findings.","agentId":"ac81190be71e37ddb"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_013RyFL7KeXnhue2VoKZaSY3","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01VqFLFYAU1sv1chDcEPiXGY","uuid":"7a2416aa-2c05-4d8c-8c7a-cb1b459c0f39","timestamp":"2026-02-28T15:28:03.265Z"}
{"parentUuid":"7a2416aa-2c05-4d8c-8c7a-cb1b459c0f39","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0156K4tyu2oaiunTFKkdv8Az","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Play.app iOS design tool SwiftUI export createwithplay.com\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Play · Design and ship mobile apps with the power of iOS & SwiftUI\",\"url\":\"https://createwithplay.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Play for iOS Engineers - Play · Design mobile apps with the power of iOS & SwiftUI\",\"url\":\"https://createwithplay.com/blog/play-for-engineers\"},{\"title\":\"Exporting SwiftUI Code | Play's Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://learn.createwithplay.com/en/articles/8500289-exporting-swiftui-code\"},{\"title\":\"Export Prototypes - Createwithplay\",\"url\":\"https://docs.createwithplay.com/en/articles/dev-handoff\"},{\"title\":\"Play to Xcode · Design mobile apps with the power of iOS & SwiftUI\",\"url\":\"https://createwithplay.com/play-to-xcode\"},{\"title\":\"Mobile App Design · Play\",\"url\":\"https://createwithplay.com/features/design\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - CreateWithPlayApp/PlaySDK\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CreateWithPlayApp/PlaySDK\"},{\"title\":\"Exporting your Play Project to Xcode | Play's Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://learn.createwithplay.com/en/articles/10752714-exporting-your-play-project-to-xcode\"},{\"title\":\"The Code Panel | Play's Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://learn.createwithplay.com/en/articles/11014038-the-code-panel\"},{\"title\":\"Play to Xcode for Individuals · Design, prototype, and ship your project to the App Store with Play.\",\"url\":\"https://createwithplay.com/play-to-xcode/individuals\"}]\n\nI've found comprehensive information about Play.app and its SwiftUI export capabilities from createwithplay.com. Here's what the search reveals:\n\n## Overview\n\nPlay is a native design tool for iOS, as opposed to a traditional vector-based drawing tool, and it allows designers to work with SwiftUI directly.\n\n## SwiftUI Export Features\n\nPlay offers two primary ways to export designs to Xcode:\n\n1. **Play to Xcode (SDK)**: This allows you to move your project from Play to Xcode without writing additional code, exporting everything you've created as a complete Swift package. Play to Xcode takes everything you've created in Play—pages and components (including interactions), assets, styles, and variables—and exports them as a Swift package that can be directly integrated into your Xcode project.\n\n2. **SwiftUI Code Panel**: This provides SwiftUI code, properties, and hierarchy as a reference guide for developers familiar with Xcode and SwiftUI code.\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\n- Export styles, components, full pages & flows directly to Xcode\n- Engineers can easily copy the code to lay out views in Xcode, saving them a ton of time\n- Play generates highly performant native UIKit or SwiftUI code that integrates seamlessly with your existing projects and can be safely shipped to production\n\n## Important Note\n\nStarting April 20, 2026, Play will no longer support the Play iOS and macOS apps, though existing exports and SDKs will continue to function.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4d9b9cca-e385-45e8-a1ae-a296db838c45","timestamp":"2026-02-28T15:28:06.139Z"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"Research Play.app (createwithplay.com / play.app) — the iOS native design tool that exports SwiftUI. I need to know:\n\n1. What UI component library does Play provide? (cards, buttons, navigation, lists, etc.)\n2. How does the SwiftUI export work — what format, any dependencies?\n3. Can Play components be used in a Swift Playground App (.swiftpm) project directly?\n4. Any known limitations of Play's exported SwiftUI code?\n5. Does Play have a package/framework that can be added as a dependency, or is it purely copy-paste export?\n\nFocus on practical integration details, not marketing. Return concise findings.","agentId":"ac81190be71e37ddb"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_013RyFL7KeXnhue2VoKZaSY3","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01VqFLFYAU1sv1chDcEPiXGY","uuid":"7bd1561b-2d28-4ab0-9546-43ea0ce12a03","timestamp":"2026-02-28T15:28:06.140Z"}
{"parentUuid":"7bd1561b-2d28-4ab0-9546-43ea0ce12a03","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S5AF1teQK5nGmqkir7MPvz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Play.app exported SwiftUI code format dependencies\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Exporting SwiftUI Code | Play's Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://learn.createwithplay.com/en/articles/8500289-exporting-swiftui-code\"},{\"title\":\"Adding Swift package dependencies in Xcode - a free Hacking with iOS: SwiftUI Edition tutorial\",\"url\":\"https://www.hackingwithswift.com/books/ios-swiftui/adding-swift-package-dependencies-in-xcode\"},{\"title\":\"Exporting Your Design in SwiftUI Code\",\"url\":\"https://learn.createwithplay.com/en/articles/8500289-exporting-your-design-in-swiftui-code\"},{\"title\":\"Managing dependencies using the Swift Package Manager | Swift by Sundell\",\"url\":\"https://www.swiftbysundell.com/articles/managing-dependencies-using-the-swift-package-manager/\"},{\"title\":\"How Play to Xcode Simplifies iOS App Design-to-Development - Geeky Gadgets\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeky-gadgets.com/play-to-xcode-export-process/\"},{\"title\":\"Demystify SwiftUI - WWDC21 - Videos - Apple Developer\",\"url\":\"https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2021/10022/\"},{\"title\":\"Adopting Swift Packages in Xcode - WWDC19 - Videos - Apple Developer\",\"url\":\"https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/408/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - pointfreeco/swift-dependencies: A dependency management library inspired by SwiftUI's \\\"environment.\\\"\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pointfreeco/swift-dependencies\"},{\"title\":\"Modularizing iOS Applications with SwiftUI and Swift Package Manager - A Modern Approach – Nimble\",\"url\":\"https://nimblehq.co/blog/modern-approach-modularize-ios-swiftui-spm\"},{\"title\":\"Crafting document-based apps in SwiftUI\",\"url\":\"https://www.createwithswift.com/crafting-document-based-apps-in-swiftui/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Play.app exported SwiftUI code format dependencies:\n\n## Play.app SwiftUI Code Export\n\nPlay generates SwiftUI code for the layout based on your designs in Play. When exporting code, there are two main approaches:\n\n### Code Export Format\n\nCode can be exported from the Code Panel on macOS. Layout code populates the Code Panel in Design Mode, and Interaction code populates it in Interaction Mode. If you've copied the entire code block, Play's exported code includes the file preamble.\n\n### SDK Export with Dependencies\n\nFor more comprehensive exports with full dependencies, the Play to Xcode feature allows seamless export of designs, components, and assets from Play into Xcode as a Swift package, supporting both SwiftUI and UIKit frameworks while preserving animations and interactions.\n\nWhen using the Play to Xcode SDK export, essential assets such as fonts, images, and videos should be included in the Swift package to ensure the full integration of your design elements. This export is a package that includes pages, components, variables, assets, and styles, not written SwiftUI code. If you need SwiftUI code for reference, you can check out the code panel.\n\nThe key distinction is that the code panel export provides generated SwiftUI code as reference, while the Play to Xcode SDK export creates a Swift package with all dependencies properly configured for integration into your Xcode project.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6632627f-fb91-409d-b2da-dcaa9196b7e2","timestamp":"2026-02-28T15:28:06.338Z"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"Research Play.app (createwithplay.com / play.app) — the iOS native design tool that exports SwiftUI. I need to know:\n\n1. What UI component library does Play provide? (cards, buttons, navigation, lists, etc.)\n2. How does the SwiftUI export work — what format, any dependencies?\n3. Can Play components be used in a Swift Playground App (.swiftpm) project directly?\n4. Any known limitations of Play's exported SwiftUI code?\n5. Does Play have a package/framework that can be added as a dependency, or is it purely copy-paste export?\n\nFocus on practical integration details, not marketing. Return concise findings.","agentId":"ac81190be71e37ddb"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_013RyFL7KeXnhue2VoKZaSY3","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01VqFLFYAU1sv1chDcEPiXGY","uuid":"4caf9aab-f27d-4891-83b6-6b65b12d4a55","timestamp":"2026-02-28T15:28:06.338Z"}
