{"parentUuid":"7c2704e0-4198-4dec-91b1-5880cabc3928","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01THQTqdrHTfdHZ6h1WU7DDi","type":"tool_result","content":"REDIRECT DETECTED: The URL redirects to a different host.\n\nOriginal URL: https://learn.createwithplay.com/en/articles/8500289-exporting-swiftui-code\nRedirect URL: https://docs.createwithplay.com/\nStatus: 302 Found\n\nTo complete your request, I need to fetch content from the redirected URL. Please use WebFetch again with these parameters:\n- url: \"https://docs.createwithplay.com/\"\n- prompt: \"What UI components does Play support? What is the format and structure of exported SwiftUI code?\""}]},"uuid":"d7ac1d2d-cebe-462b-b23e-e9d13c0524f5","timestamp":"2026-02-28T15:28:14.136Z"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"Research Play.app (createwithplay.com / play.app) — the iOS native design tool that exports SwiftUI. I need to know:\n\n1. What UI component library does Play provide? (cards, buttons, navigation, lists, etc.)\n2. How does the SwiftUI export work — what format, any dependencies?\n3. Can Play components be used in a Swift Playground App (.swiftpm) project directly?\n4. Any known limitations of Play's exported SwiftUI code?\n5. Does Play have a package/framework that can be added as a dependency, or is it purely copy-paste export?\n\nFocus on practical integration details, not marketing. Return concise findings.","agentId":"ac81190be71e37ddb"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_013RyFL7KeXnhue2VoKZaSY3","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01VqFLFYAU1sv1chDcEPiXGY","uuid":"379d4422-04b4-4f9b-bc78-f861a4c34f1c","timestamp":"2026-02-28T15:28:14.138Z"}
{"parentUuid":"379d4422-04b4-4f9b-bc78-f861a4c34f1c","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VLac4HfLQA5r3bTAdpyXcx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Play app PlaySDK GitHub swift package components\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - CreateWithPlayApp/PlaySDK\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CreateWithPlayApp/PlaySDK\"},{\"title\":\"Play to Xcode lets you turn mockups into real apps\",\"url\":\"https://9to5mac.com/2025/04/18/play-to-xcode-mockups-into-real-apps/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - alemohamad/swift-playground-app-structure: Package App Structure in Swift Playgrounds\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/alemohamad/swift-playground-app-structure\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - piemonte/Player: ▶️ Play and stream media in Swift\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/piemonte/Player\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ybrid/player-sdk-swift: Audio Player SDK written in Swift, fully compatible with Ybrid®. Can be used in iOS, iPadOS, etc., or other Swift applications.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ybrid/player-sdk-swift\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - apple/swift-play-experimental\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/apple/swift-play-experimental\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - apptreesoftware/playsdk: AppTree SDK for the Play Framework\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/apptreesoftware/playsdk\"},{\"title\":\"audio-player · GitHub Topics\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/topics/audio-player?l=swift\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - swiftlang/swift-android-examples\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/swiftlang/swift-android-examples\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - toph42/ExampleKit: This is an example of how to develop a library in Swift Playgrounds 4 on iPad and deploy it such that it can be added as a Package to other Swift Playgrounds App projects.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/toph42/ExampleKit\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about PlaySDK from the Play app on GitHub. Here's what I found:\n\n## PlaySDK Overview\n\nPlaySDK is a Swift Package available in both UIKit and SwiftUI that includes fonts, assets, colors, variables, Components and Pages saved in Play, and enables your Play designs to be rendered as native code.\n\n## Key Components\n\nPlaySDK includes UI components like Chip, which can be instantiated in your application with different states (such as 'defaultState' and 'selected') and supports state change callbacks.\n\n## Integration\n\nYou can instantiate a component in your existing application by importing your package. During the export process, Play gives you the option to add your project to an existing app by selecting Publish, then Export New Project, and choosing an existing Xcode project, and Play will automatically add the necessary packages and entitlements to your existing project.\n\n## Example Project\n\nAn example project is included in the repository that demonstrates how to integrate Play components and pages into an Xcode project.\n\nThe PlaySDK repository is available at: https://github.com/CreateWithPlayApp/PlaySDK\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3148bbf0-afa4-42c1-91e0-92ef7eba4fa0","timestamp":"2026-02-28T15:28:20.415Z"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"Research Play.app (createwithplay.com / play.app) — the iOS native design tool that exports SwiftUI. I need to know:\n\n1. What UI component library does Play provide? (cards, buttons, navigation, lists, etc.)\n2. How does the SwiftUI export work — what format, any dependencies?\n3. Can Play components be used in a Swift Playground App (.swiftpm) project directly?\n4. Any known limitations of Play's exported SwiftUI code?\n5. Does Play have a package/framework that can be added as a dependency, or is it purely copy-paste export?\n\nFocus on practical integration details, not marketing. Return concise findings.","agentId":"ac81190be71e37ddb"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_013RyFL7KeXnhue2VoKZaSY3","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01VqFLFYAU1sv1chDcEPiXGY","uuid":"acd0d5a9-b5a9-45f3-a002-190c460f525e","timestamp":"2026-02-28T15:28:20.415Z"}
{"parentUuid":"acd0d5a9-b5a9-45f3-a002-190c460f525e","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FaMcMaEJmjdLQ8BpuTZtEW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Play.app\" SwiftUI Playground .swiftpm compatibility\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Swift Playgrounds App Projects | Aaron Sky\",\"url\":\"https://skyaaron.com/posts/swiftpm-app-projects/\"},{\"title\":\"Setting Up Your Swift Playground App Project | by Ryan Du | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://ryendu.medium.com/setting-up-your-swift-playground-app-project-cb32a0fd6e62\"},{\"title\":\"Playground Support | Apple Developer Forums\",\"url\":\"https://developer.apple.com/forums/tags/playground-support\"},{\"title\":\"Swift Playground App - App Store\",\"url\":\"https://apps.apple.REDACTED\"},{\"title\":\"Swift Playground - Apple Developer\",\"url\":\"https://developer.apple.com/swift-playground/\"},{\"title\":\"How to use SwiftUI in Swift Playgrounds – Hacking with Swift\",\"url\":\"https://www.hackingwithswift.com/articles/203/how-to-use-swiftui-in-swift-playgrounds\"},{\"title\":\"Swift Playground | Apple Developer Forums\",\"url\":\"https://developer.apple.com/forums/tags/swift-playground?page=3\"},{\"title\":\"Build a SwiftUI view in Swift Playgrounds - WWDC20 - Videos - Apple Developer\",\"url\":\"https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2020/10643/\"},{\"title\":\"Is it possible to developer a SwiftUI app using only SwiftPM? - Using Swift - Swift Forums\",\"url\":\"https://forums.swift.org/t/is-it-possible-to-developer-a-swiftui-app-using-only-swiftpm/71755\"},{\"title\":\"Creating Your First App using SwiftUI in Playgrounds - Apple Education Community\",\"url\":\"https://education.apple.com/resource/250010796\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Play.app, SwiftUI Playground, and .swiftpm compatibility:\n\n## Swift Playground Apps and .swiftpm Format\n\nSwift Playground Projects are based on the manifest description format used with Swift Packages, with project manifests and their source files entirely contained in a \"package\" with the extension *.swiftpm.\n\nSwift Playground Apps only support SwiftUI, and they can be exported directly from Swift Playgrounds as a .swiftpm file.\n\n## Compatibility with Xcode\n\nThe new Swift Playgrounds App Project format shares a compatibility story with Xcode. These projects are backed by Swift Package Manager.\n\n## SwiftUI Support\n\nWith Swift Playground you build apps using SwiftUI, the powerful, modern user interface framework. With support for Swift Packages, Swift Playground makes it easier to code your creations, as packages are bundles of reusable code that can be included in your projects.\n\nThe .swiftpm format represents a significant development because it allows Swift Playgrounds to leverage Swift Package Manager infrastructure while providing a unified format that works across both iPad/Mac Swift Playgrounds and Xcode environments.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4a428c69-eba1-4568-84f4-4c68bd3225cb","timestamp":"2026-02-28T15:28:23.634Z"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"Research Play.app (createwithplay.com / play.app) — the iOS native design tool that exports SwiftUI. I need to know:\n\n1. What UI component library does Play provide? (cards, buttons, navigation, lists, etc.)\n2. How does the SwiftUI export work — what format, any dependencies?\n3. Can Play components be used in a Swift Playground App (.swiftpm) project directly?\n4. Any known limitations of Play's exported SwiftUI code?\n5. Does Play have a package/framework that can be added as a dependency, or is it purely copy-paste export?\n\nFocus on practical integration details, not marketing. Return concise findings.","agentId":"ac81190be71e37ddb"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_013RyFL7KeXnhue2VoKZaSY3","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01VqFLFYAU1sv1chDcEPiXGY","uuid":"358b0ba3-9cb1-4162-9a1b-ce4858b377a8","timestamp":"2026-02-28T15:28:23.634Z"}
